[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: The renderer: a content-blind page over one payload, keyed on tree shape and widget words

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-VIEW-RENDERER
TITLE: The renderer: a content-blind page over one payload, keyed on tree shape and widget words
DEPTH: interface-settled
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
render.py takes one payload and one template and writes one self-contained
page; it refuses any payload whose schema it was not built for. The page:
Start shows the root's own prose, the legend and the check findings, count
first; one tab per child of the root, in order; a tab with children shows
them as sections in order and a section with children shows cards; a
narrative without children draws its own widget; a last tab, Nodes, lists
every cited node grouped by type with its state, its backlinks and its
relations, and gives each node a screen of its own with its neighbours.
Widgets: prose, rows (with the legend's colour on the bracket word and the
count of rows per word above the list), table, glossary (term cards),
legend, tally (bars of backlink counts per child, totals first), edges
(the pairs as a diagram, counts on the arrows). Every UID is shown with its
title. Colour is only ever a legend word and is always written out beside
it. The page renders in both themes.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The screens are an opinion about shape, allowed by REQ-VIEW-RENDERER-IS-CONTENT-BLIND; a project whose root has no legend simply has no colours.
<<<
